NKAS changes to the ADB build select only linked libraries, remove duplicate
compilation units, supply generated protobuf headers, and provide an
application-owned server startup entry point. The embedded server rejects
kill-server and does not install the command-line SIGINT/atexit handlers or
scan for local emulators. See native/adb/embedded.patch for the modifications.

NKAS groups Abseil's Apple architecture flags so CMake preserves each selector
with its compiler option. See native/adb/abseil-apple.patch.

The Android build downloads and verifies the scrcpy server when the bundled
asset is missing. The iOS Runner includes the same v4.1 server asset so the
foreground scrcpy session does not depend on an external installation.
